		<bioghist encodinganalog="545">
			<head>Biographical Note </head>
			<p>Rudolph Ruzicka (1883–1978) was an artist known for his engraving, typeface design,
				illustrations and other work in the book world.</p>
		</bioghist>
		<scopecontent encodinganalog="520">
			<head>Scope and Content Note</head>
			<p>Primarily printed material (greeting cards, pamphlets, programs) relating to or
				including Ruzicka's work. Of particular note is the work he did for Vassar College
				for the 50th anniversary of the opening of the college. Included are 11 of the 12
				original drawings for the woodcuts used in <emph render="underline">Sketches of
					Vassar College</emph>.</p>
		</scopecontent>
